 "description": "<p>Itilleq (old spelling: Itivdleq) is a settlement in the Qeqqata municipality in central-western Greenland. It is located on a small island around 1 km from the mainland, 45 km south of Sisimiut[2] and 2 km north of the Arctic Circle on the shores of Davis Strait. It had 112 inhabitants in 2010. Source: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Itilleq\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a></p><p>For further information (in Danish) see also the Danish Geodata Agency:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.gronlandskehavnelods.dk/#HID=32\" target=\"_blank\">Den grønlandske Havnelods</a></p>",
